{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.canonical","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.lean#L92-L121","doc":"**The trivial model — a `def`, not an `instance`, and not \"faithful\".**\n\nIts docstring said *\"Faithful instance. Carries the explicit research-grade\nconjecture as a sorry.\"* Neither half was true. There is no `sorry`: it sets\n`barInvolution T := T`, so `bar_invariant` is discharged by `rfl` on\n`T = T`. Every normal form is bar-invariant because the bar involution is\nthe identity map — nothing here sends `q ↦ q⁻¹` or reverses a crossing, and\n`bar_involutive` is `rfl` for the same reason. A `sorry` would at least be\nvisible to `#print axioms`; this was not.\n\nAs an unconditional `instance` it made `barInvolution_eq_self` and\n`nodeOf_barInvolution_highest_weight` unconditional theorems about the\nidentity map, so `conj:symmetric-crystal-pair-production` asserted nothing.\n\nDemoted the same way as `ConfinementGradingCorrespondence.canonical`\n(bean `qou-fngs`). Nothing consumed it: the class has no users outside this\nfile.\n\n**Still open:** that the GS-generated normal forms are fixed by the genuine\nbar involution, and the Type-B folding statement that a transition\n`v₀ → v₋ ⊔ v₊` out of a bar-invariant source produces a bar-conjugate\npair — which no field of this class states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.nodeOf_barInvolution_highest_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.nodeOf_barInvolution_highest_weight","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.lean#L74-L90","doc":"**Conditional theorem (CPT pairing on highest-weight vectors).**\n\nAssuming both `[CrystalGraphRealization R q]` and\n`[SymmetricCrystalPairProduction R q]`: the bar-image of any GS\nnormal form has the same crystal node as the original, and is\ntherefore also a Kashiwara highest-weight vector.  This is the\nLean shadow of the bar-conjugate det-law identity and the\nstructural CPT-pairing observation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.barInvolution_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.barInvolution_idem","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.lean#L64-L72","doc":"Bar-involution-twice is the identity (corollary of involutivity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.barInvolution_eq_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.barInvolution_eq_self","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.lean#L53-L62","doc":"Unconditional structural lemma: bar-involution acts as the\nidentity on every normal form.  Direct from `bar_invariant`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.lean#L49-L49","doc":"**The conjecture itself**: every GS normal form is\nbar-invariant.  Plays the role of `sorry`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.bar_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.bar_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Bar-involution is involutive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.barInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.barInvolution","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Bar-involution on normal forms `T_w ↦ T̄_w` (sends `q ↦ q⁻¹`\nand reverses crossings). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction","kind":"class","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.lean#L29-L49","doc":"**Symmetric-crystal pair production (conjecture).**\n\nEncodes Type-B folding of the `𝔰𝔩_n` crystal: every transition\n`v_0 → v_- ⊔ v_+` from a bar-invariant source produces a\nbar-conjugate pair, and every normal form generated by the GS\nengine is bar-invariant. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:symmetric-crystal-pair-production","label":"conj:symmetric-crystal-pair-production","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/symmetric-crystal-pair-production.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}